.DS_Store
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.env*.local
.vercel
**/.next/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/.tmp/

# Claude Code: session-local runtime state is ignored, but the project's permission
# rules (settings.json), agent definitions, and skills are committed so they bind every
# agent working in this repo.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/

# Third-party skills fetched by `npx skills add` (see .claude/skills/*'s symlinks). Reinstalled
# from the command each SKILL.md documents, not checked in.
.agents
skills-lock.json

# Supplier deliverable — copied into docs/design/ and packages/three-adapter/reference/,
# deleted from the working tree once the port is finished. Nothing may depend on it.
design-source/

# `next dev` regenerates apps/web/AGENTS.md and apps/web/CLAUDE.md whenever it detects an AI
# coding agent (next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js, gated on getAgentName()). It keys
# on the Next project directory, so a root-level AGENTS.md cannot satisfy it and there is no
# config opt-out. This repository keeps exactly ONE tracked pair, at the root: agent guidance is
# routed from there, and a second file under apps/web would silently split it.
apps/web/AGENTS.md
apps/web/CLAUDE.md

# Generated by Next.js, and it flips with the build mode: `next build` writes
# `./.next/types/...` into it, `next dev` writes `./.next/dev/types/...`. Tracked, it produced a
# spurious diff on every switch between the two. The `typecheck` gate runs before `build` and
# survives its absence on a fresh clone — `apps/web/tsconfig.json` lists it under `include`, and
# TypeScript tolerates an include entry that matches no file. Verified by deleting it and running
# `pnpm typecheck` (exit 0) before untracking.
apps/web/next-env.d.ts

# Playwright MCP session artifacts (console logs, page snapshots) — evidence, not source.
.playwright-mcp/

# Review and visual artefacts written by agent runs — evidence, not source. The
# whole directory is untracked as of 2026-09-07, including the ten adversarial
# reports committed in August; screenshots alone reached 17 MB in one pass.
#
# They are still cited by name from about twenty accepted ADRs and from
# `docs/milestones/adversarial-review-remediation.md`. Those citations now point
# at git history rather than at a checked-out file: `git log --all -- <path>`
# finds the commit, `git show <commit>:<path>` prints it.
testing-reports/
.env*
